  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nFrontal passage will signal an end to widespread precipitation \nlate in the week as the surface low gradually fills and tracks \neast across the Great Lakes. Lingering low-level cyclonic flow \nand wrap-around moisture within post-frontal CAA will maintain \nstratocumulus clouds along with isolated sprinkles or light \nshowers Thursday and Friday. Highs late week will cool into the \n50s in spots. GFS and ECMWF suggest another fast-moving \nshortwave may clip the region over the weekend, though details \nremain uncertain. NBM currently maintains a baseline 15-20% PoP \nfor Sunday.",
